{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam al-Reza (a.s.)",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nيَا صَاحِبِي فِي شِدَّتِي\nYAA SAAHIBEE FEE SHIDDATEE\nO My Companion in my distress!\nوَيَا وَلِيِّي فِي نِعْمَتِي\nWA YAA WALIYYEE FEE NI'MATEE\nO My Patron in my bounties!\nوَيَا اِلٰهِي وَاِلٰهَ اِبْرَاهِيمَ وَاِسْمَاعِيلَ\nWA YAA ILAAHEE WA ILAAHA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAA'EEL\nO My God and the God of Abraham, Ishmael,\nوَاِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ\nWA ISHAAQA WA YA'QOOB\nIsaac, and Jacob!\nيَا رَبَّ كٓهٰيٰعٓصٓ وَيٰسٓ وَالْقُرْآنِ الْحَكِيمِ\nYAA RABBA KAAAF HAA YAA A'YN SAAAD WA YAA SEEN WAL QUR'AANIL HAKEEM\nO Lord of Kaf-Ha-Ya-'Ayn-Sad, Ya-Sin, and the Qur'an full of wisdom!\nاَسْاَلُكَ يَا اَحْسَنَ مَنْ سُئِلَ\nAS'ALUKA YAA AHSANA MAN SU'IL\nI beseech You, O Most Excellent of all those who may be besought!\nوَيَا خَيْرَ مَنْ دُعِيَ\nWA YAA KHAYRA MAN DU'IY\nO Most Favorite of all those who may be prayed!\nوَيَا اَجْوَدَ مَنْ اَعْطَىٰ\nWA YAA AJWADA MAN A'TAA\nO Most Magnanimous of all those who may give!\nوَيَا خَيْرَ مُرْتَجىٰ\nWA YAA KHAYRA MURTAJAA\nO Most Preferred of all those who may be hoped!\nاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS'ALUKA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nI beseech You to send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has recorded a special prayer and supplication for each of the Holy Imams (a.s.), to be offered on Fridays.\nImam al-Reza (a.s.)'s prayer consists of six units. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Insan](A80) ten times."
}
